      "id": "white",
      "name": "Fawn",
      "description": "Round, oval or tapered spots in one consecutive run somewhere between the neck and the rump - never two clusters with a gap between them, never a spiral or a pattern, just a flowing line of them. They keep off the face, the belly and the legs. Most fawn horses also carry a stylised white eyeliner, a slightly darkened topline in the manner of sooty, a pangare-like lightening underneath, and a pale underside to the tail. Every white on the horse is the same white. Blue eyes are possible.",
